(759360, 81249, 19608, '<td valign="top">Wonderful scene.  Shadow is perfect - it makes the shot.  Even though the sun is close to the horizon - the sky is a bit over powering.  Try a graduated ND filter - it''s made for scenes like this.  One of my top 10 pics.</td>', 'Wonderful scene.  Shadow is perfect - it makes the shot.  Even though the sun is close to the horizon - the sky is a bit over powering.  Try a graduated ND filter - it''s made for scenes like this.  One of my top 10 pics.', '2004-06-11 03:22:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(759364, 82489, 19608, '<td valign="top">So simple yet so effective.  Your gradation from black close to the model''s head to ligher blue of the left edge is an absolute masterpiece of execution.  The lighting on your (beautiful) model''s face is exceptional.  And she really does have the expression of "waiting for inspiration."  Composition - perfect for text on the left side - and also visually appealing.  Q.  What don''t I like?  A.  It''s not mine.</td>', 'So simple yet so effective.  Your gradation from black close to the model''s head to ligher blue of the left edge is an absolute masterpiece of execution.  The lighting on your (beautiful) model''s face is exceptional.  And she really does have the expression of "waiting for inspiration."  Composition - perfect for text on the left side - and also visually appealing.  Q.  What don''t I like?  A.  It''s not mine.', '2004-06-11 03:28:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(759368, 81737, 19608, '<td valign="top">You have a wonderful image, great colors - great silhouette.  But I think the person you were shoooting with did a better job for "waiting" with the fishing angle ("Fisherman''s Patience.")   Both images are great, but if I had to pick one over the other....  I don''t know which has the horizontalk flip - but like the larger black area on the left side.  This one (and the other one) is one of my top picks.</td>', 'You have a wonderful image, great colors - great silhouette.  But I think the person you were shoooting with did a better job for "waiting" with the fishing angle ("Fisherman''s Patience.")   Both images are great, but if I had to pick one over the other....  I don''t know which has the horizontalk flip - but like the larger black area on the left side.  This one (and the other one) is one of my top picks.', '2004-06-11 03:39:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(759416, 82275, 20395, '<td valign="top">This could be a very good pic, but it''s too small to tell! Please use the maxium size you can when entering next time!</td>', 'This could be a very good pic, but it''s too small to tell! Please use the maxium size you can when entering next time!', '2004-06-11 06:10:54.000000', NULL, 1),
