(764845, 81270, 17203, '<td valign="top">I thought it was a good shot and gave it a 7. The composition was very good, but the light is a little flat, and it doesn''t <i>express</i> waiting as well as some other shots did. Without reading the title, the wait aspect is kind of obscure.</td>', 'I thought it was a good shot and gave it a 7. The composition was very good, but the light is a little flat, and it doesn''t express waiting as well as some other shots did. Without reading the title, the wait aspect is kind of obscure.', '2004-06-16 01:11:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(764846, 81270, 20809, '<td valign="top">I gave you a 6. Sorry, It does not POP like some others in the challenge.  Seems a little dark to me, and maybe could use better cropping?  The fence on the right is distracting.  IMHO I am new to this...</td>', 'I gave you a 6. Sorry, It does not POP like some others in the challenge.  Seems a little dark to me, and maybe could use better cropping?  The fence on the right is distracting.  IMHO I am new to this...', '2004-06-16 01:11:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(764849, 81154, 22166, '<td valign="top">Hello, All<br/>Thank you for your comments.  As this is my first entry, I did not expect it to do well.<br/>The three major concerns addressed through the comments were;<br/> <br/>1. Foreground too hot&gt; Lush as it might seem, Reno is still a desert<br/>and dry desert soil can sometimes be highly reflective.  That''s nature.  <br/>No spot editing. Those are the rules.  You never know, could be the hot foreground helped cut the flash enough to keep the subjects from getting blown away.  However,<br/>I could have cropped it right down to the hole but then wed be looking at res issues and the border of what constitutes spot editing. (as in, if asked to provide the original)<br/> <br/>2. Focus on the "kids" too soft&gt; Inside the hole it''s dark. The focus was a guess, O.K.?  A quarter inch either way or half a stop?<br/> <br/>3. Getting the shot&gt; Sometimes I think I inherited some of my Uncle''s gift for working with animals. But then, my own dogs prove me wrong.  <br/>These squirrels were nice enough to give up a little of their playtime for me.  Not knowing when they''d break it off, I tried to get as many shots as I could. Only 2 said, waiting."<br/>This was the cutest one.  Someday, I might get to post the rest.<br/>In the meantime, I''ll keep trying.<br/>Thanks again,<br/>MD<br/>P.S. Im sure some of this could have been avoided if I had hired professional squirrels.<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-06-16 12:51:03.</i></td>', 'Hello, AllThank you for your comments.  As this is my first entry, I did not expect it to do well.The three major concerns addressed through the comments were; 1. Foreground too hot> Lush as it might seem, Reno is still a desertand dry desert soil can sometimes be highly reflective.  That''s nature.  No spot editing. Those are the rules.  You never know, could be the hot foreground helped cut the flash enough to keep the subjects from getting blown away.  However,I could have cropped it right down to the hole but then wed be looking at res issues and the border of what constitutes spot editing. (as in, if asked to provide the original) 2. Focus on the "kids" too soft> Inside the hole it''s dark. The focus was a guess, O.K.?  A quarter inch either way or half a stop? 3. Getting the shot> Sometimes I think I inherited some of my Uncle''s gift for working with animals. But then, my own dogs prove me wrong.  These squirrels were nice enough to give up a little of their playtime for me.  Not knowing when they''d break it off, I tried to get as many shots as I could. Only 2 said, waiting."This was the cutest one.  Someday, I might get to post the rest.In the meantime, I''ll keep trying.Thanks again,MDP.S. Im sure some of this could have been avoided if I had hired professional squirrels.', '2004-06-16 01:13:08.000000', '2004-06-16 13:51:03.000000', 0),
(764865, 82382, 7560, '<td valign="top">Eight 1s???! No way. This is a very solid black and white image that manages to convay a sense of waiting to anyone who''s ever waited for the last seed on a dandilion to fall. The minor distraction for me appears to be cobwebs? They don''t add to the image, and the lines they create take my  eyes away from the image focal point. Also, one of the background twigs/flowers is still too strong even with the shallow DOF. That was the only two things that kept this from being a 9. 8</td>', 'Eight 1s???! No way. This is a very solid black and white image that manages to convay a sense of waiting to anyone who''s ever waited for the last seed on a dandilion to fall. The minor distraction for me appears to be cobwebs? They don''t add to the image, and the lines they create take my  eyes away from the image focal point. Also, one of the background twigs/flowers is still too strong even with the shallow DOF. That was the only two things that kept this from being a 9. 8', '2004-06-16 01:16:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(764867, 82141, 14986, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on a ribbon in your first challenge!<br/> <br/>Ack...I thought I was commenting on a third place shot.  Oh well...still a very nice showing for your first challenge.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-06-16 15:31:47.</i></td>', 'Congratulations on a ribbon in your first challenge! Ack...I thought I was commenting on a third place shot.  Oh well...still a very nice showing for your first challenge.', '2004-06-16 01:16:51.000000', '2004-06-16 16:31:47.000000', 0),
