(766093, 82131, 19736, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by abreul:</b></div><hr/><i> how was your day in the Zoo??? hope you have fun there... but this pic is sharp. but the birds are kool </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Actually it was taken on High Island, TX. Drove about 2 hours from Houston with 2 other photographers. I wish I had brought a wide-angle lens because there were about 100 different birds.</td>', 'Originally posted by abreul: how was your day in the Zoo??? hope you have fun there... but this pic is sharp. but the birds are kool   Actually it was taken on High Island, TX. Drove about 2 hours from Houston with 2 other photographers. I wish I had brought a wide-angle lens because there were about 100 different birds.', '2004-06-16 14:08:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(766103, 82157, 255, '<td valign="top">this is interesting, poignant, to me--having just seen much the same scene in nassau last month. but i even thought at the time that it''s the same on every island have ever been--that same bittersweet sense of a paradise paradox--those that live there probably dont even see the raw beauty anymore.</td>', 'this is interesting, poignant, to me--having just seen much the same scene in nassau last month. but i even thought at the time that it''s the same on every island have ever been--that same bittersweet sense of a paradise paradox--those that live there probably dont even see the raw beauty anymore.', '2004-06-16 14:17:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(766115, 82338, 16126, '<td valign="top">Hi John, dacht al dat deze van jou was. Ken het gevoel van wachten dat hierbij hoort, mooi getroffen.</td>', 'Hi John, dacht al dat deze van jou was. Ken het gevoel van wachten dat hierbij hoort, mooi getroffen.', '2004-06-16 14:24:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(766120, 82382, 3032, '<td valign="top">Sorry Sher, I scored this a five. I didn''t get the ''waiting'', therefore was searching for the main element and because I couldn''t find it I didn''t like the composition.<br/>Now that I come back to look at how you did in the latest challenges I see a spider and its web. Now I wonder if the photo is about the spider or about the seed. Is the seed waiting to fall (or is the photographer waiting for it to fall) or is the spider waiting for a prey?<br/>In any case I''d think I''d like it more when you had used more of the frame. When I draw a diagonal from the topleft to bottomright there is very little in the left side of that. Tilting the camera a bit up and slightly to the right might have worked. But perhaps the background would suck that way. <br/>The exposure, B&amp;W tones are great! Did you use the R25 filter for this one?</td>', 'Sorry Sher, I scored this a five. I didn''t get the ''waiting'', therefore was searching for the main element and because I couldn''t find it I didn''t like the composition.Now that I come back to look at how you did in the latest challenges I see a spider and its web. Now I wonder if the photo is about the spider or about the seed. Is the seed waiting to fall (or is the photographer waiting for it to fall) or is the spider waiting for a prey?In any case I''d think I''d like it more when you had used more of the frame. When I draw a diagonal from the topleft to bottomright there is very little in the left side of that. Tilting the camera a bit up and slightly to the right might have worked. But perhaps the background would suck that way. The exposure, B&W tones are great! Did you use the R25 filter for this one?', '2004-06-16 14:26:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(766141, 81659, 3032, '<td valign="top">The use of the mirror as a compositional and storytelling tool made me stop and look a while during voting. That''s a good sign so I scored it an 8. :)<br/>This may be a bit of work, but I wonder how it would work if you had used a low reflector with gold color to bring more warmth and more light balance into this shot. It would not be visible in the mirror. The light on the arm and cheek is very harsh and cool now.</td>', 'The use of the mirror as a compositional and storytelling tool made me stop and look a while during voting. That''s a good sign so I scored it an 8. :)This may be a bit of work, but I wonder how it would work if you had used a low reflector with gold color to bring more warmth and more light balance into this shot. It would not be visible in the mirror. The light on the arm and cheek is very harsh and cool now.', '2004-06-16 14:41:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(766165, 81784, 20313, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the comments im only 17 and just started out at photography any criticisms are excepted and i will use them to make my tecnique more consistant. <br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks for the comments im only 17 and just started out at photography any criticisms are excepted and i will use them to make my tecnique more consistant.  ', '2004-06-16 15:02:47.000000', NULL, 0),
