(766519, 81737, 2741, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by TabbyCat:</b></div><hr/><i> Eek! Okay, so I was totally wrong about guessing you to be Nazgul... ;-) But take it as a compliment, as he creates terrific photographs and this photograph is a terrific one also! Congratulations! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Gee... thats the same thing you said to the first place winner, but only changed the name. Do you say this of everyone??</td>', 'Originally posted by TabbyCat: Eek! Okay, so I was totally wrong about guessing you to be Nazgul... ;-) But take it as a compliment, as he creates terrific photographs and this photograph is a terrific one also! Congratulations!   Gee... thats the same thing you said to the first place winner, but only changed the name. Do you say this of everyone??', '2004-06-16 18:24:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(766607, 82362, 9452, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by heidarthor:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by crazycrystal1977:</b></div><hr/><i> DID YOU NOTICE THAT FIRST AND THIRD PLACES LOOK WAY TOO CLOSE!!! Looks like the same lake..same time..different angle. Not good... </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>This is very weird! It looks like one of them has been flipped vertically. The stones in the lower right corner on the first place one are the same as the stones in the lower left corner of the one in third place. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>And same camera!!!</td>', 'Originally posted by heidarthor: Originally posted by crazycrystal1977: DID YOU NOTICE THAT FIRST AND THIRD PLACES LOOK WAY TOO CLOSE!!! Looks like the same lake..same time..different angle. Not good...   This is very weird! It looks like one of them has been flipped vertically. The stones in the lower right corner on the first place one are the same as the stones in the lower left corner of the one in third place.   And same camera!!!', '2004-06-16 18:50:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(766629, 82446, 22166, '<td valign="top">Hi.  Just to set the record straight,  Cameras are an individual casino decision.  Some may still not allow cameras period.  Some might ban video only.  But in the last 5 or 6 years many casinos realize a cam ban is just bad P.R. and almost impossible to enforce.  Technology also renders such bans moot and we digi owners know.  The security people WILL get interested in you if you spend too much time on a particular area.</td>', 'Hi.  Just to set the record straight,  Cameras are an individual casino decision.  Some may still not allow cameras period.  Some might ban video only.  But in the last 5 or 6 years many casinos realize a cam ban is just bad P.R. and almost impossible to enforce.  Technology also renders such bans moot and we digi owners know.  The security people WILL get interested in you if you spend too much time on a particular area.', '2004-06-16 18:55:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(766721, 81559, 14614, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all for comments -- yes, it IS cropped too tight.  I appreciate the confirmation.<br/> <br/>I found myself in a photographer''s dilemma as I had a great shot of this fellow and his partner waiting for the next customer.  At the "eleventh" hour I decided to recrop it because you could identify the partner (I wouldn''t want someone to post my shot so I didn''t want to post his)  I tried the crop and thought it still communicated waiting.</td>', 'Thanks to all for comments -- yes, it IS cropped too tight.  I appreciate the confirmation. I found myself in a photographer''s dilemma as I had a great shot of this fellow and his partner waiting for the next customer.  At the "eleventh" hour I decided to recrop it because you could identify the partner (I wouldn''t want someone to post my shot so I didn''t want to post his)  I tried the crop and thought it still communicated waiting.', '2004-06-16 20:16:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(767045, 82295, 2109, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by abreul:</b></div><hr/><i> wy didnt you focus the thing dude... it as moving to fast? lol </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Ever seen tight focus before?</td>', 'Originally posted by abreul: wy didnt you focus the thing dude... it as moving to fast? lol   Ever seen tight focus before?', '2004-06-16 23:55:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(767046, 82295, 2109, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by slingshot:</b></div><hr/><i> out of focus head cost two points and waiting is a stretch. gave it a 5 </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>That would be the tail out of focus, and apparently you didn''t learn in elementary school that caterpillars eventually turn into butterflies.. hence, the "wait".</td>', 'Originally posted by slingshot: out of focus head cost two points and waiting is a stretch. gave it a 5   That would be the tail out of focus, and apparently you didn''t learn in elementary school that caterpillars eventually turn into butterflies.. hence, the "wait".', '2004-06-16 23:56:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(767047, 82295, 2109, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ohyea:</b></div><hr/><i> Blurred tail end (low depth of field?) seems to imply motion, so sense of waiting is gone. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Caterpillars turn into butterflies (or moths) after a period of time.  That would be the "wait".</td>', 'Originally posted by ohyea: Blurred tail end (low depth of field?) seems to imply motion, so sense of waiting is gone.   Caterpillars turn into butterflies (or moths) after a period of time.  That would be the "wait".', '2004-06-16 23:58:08.000000', NULL, 0),
