(767152, 82260, 14386, '<td valign="top">This is what I''m WAITING for...another ribbon.  OOpppsss sorry...can not contain my happiness. <br/> <br/>Yesterday, when I learned that I earned another 4th Place (my fourth 4th place), I told myself that life indeed is a waiting game...that I might wait for another ribbon... maybe forever. But the wait was rather short.<br/> <br/>I am very happy for Katrina, too, my model.  My "Strength" entry here:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=69231" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/207/thumb/69231.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/207/thumb/69231.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/207/thumb/69231.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>also placed in the top 10 and was a subject of discussion.  She said that she is a jinx to me. Well, I don''t think so. I couldn''t have a more effective model than her.<br/> <br/>Anyway, I took this shot after a Sunday mass. Hoping to join the challenge, I bought my camera to the church with the intention to take photos of kids waiting for their parents. It rained during the mass. An  idea came to me. I hope I could see a glass window with clearly visible raindrops. Katrina was a given; she is a parishioner of the church. Then I saw what I was looking for. I took around 20 shots and this was one of them.<br/> <br/>Thanks to your votes. This ribbon makes my week!<br/> <br/>Manny<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-06-17 00:56:39.</i></td>', 'This is what I''m WAITING for...another ribbon.  OOpppsss sorry...can not contain my happiness.  Yesterday, when I learned that I earned another 4th Place (my fourth 4th place), I told myself that life indeed is a waiting game...that I might wait for another ribbon... maybe forever. But the wait was rather short. I am very happy for Katrina, too, my model.  My "Strength" entry here:   also placed in the top 10 and was a subject of discussion.  She said that she is a jinx to me. Well, I don''t think so. I couldn''t have a more effective model than her. Anyway, I took this shot after a Sunday mass. Hoping to join the challenge, I bought my camera to the church with the intention to take photos of kids waiting for their parents. It rained during the mass. An  idea came to me. I hope I could see a glass window with clearly visible raindrops. Katrina was a given; she is a parishioner of the church. Then I saw what I was looking for. I took around 20 shots and this was one of them. Thanks to your votes. This ribbon makes my week! Manny', '2004-06-17 01:52:35.000000', '2004-06-17 01:56:39.000000', 0),
